# path: /v1/asr/transcribe
# base-url: https://api.meta.ai   (export META_BASE_URL=https://api.meta.ai ; the path above carries /v1)
# content-type: multipart
# file-field: audio
# file-type: audio/wav
# accept: application/json
# model: muse-voice-transcribe-1.0
# verified: https://dev.meta.ai/docs/api-reference/voice/transcribe + .../voice/schemas + https://dev.meta.ai/docs/speech-to-text
#   (2026-10-28): multipart/form-data with two parts: "request" (JSON, type application/json) and "audio" (the clip).
#   audioEncoding must be "WAV": RIFF/WAVE, mono, 16-bit PCM at 16 kHz or 24 kHz (raw PCM is rejected -> 400).
#   mode PUSH_TO_TALK (default, whole clip = one turn) | ENDPOINTING | DIARIZATION. Max 10 min / 32 MB.
#   Reply (Accept: application/json): {"sessionId", "transcript", "audioDurationMs", "turns":[...]} — "text" is NOT
#   a field. Price $0.18 per audio hour. Realtime variant: wss://api.meta.ai/v1/asr/realtime.
# unverified: Kazakh is NOT among the 25 evaluated languages (nor is Russian); languageBias takes language NAMES
#   ("Kazakh"), is only a hint, and an unknown name degrades to auto-detect. Expect the Day 1 gate to fail here
#   unless the clip is short and clear; cut line 1 (Voice) is the fallback.
# unverified: optional "keywords": ["секір", ...] biasing on Kazakh command words — try it on the second probe.
{
  "request": {
    "model": "muse-voice-transcribe-1.0",
    "audioEncoding": "WAV",
    "mode": "PUSH_TO_TALK",
    "languageBias": ["Kazakh"]
  }
}
